  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improvements to FAO Headquarters Facilities</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The scope of the MoU between FAO and Italy is to facilitate a way for the latter to provide funds for the implementation of the USD 40million Masterplan study prepared in year 2014 by the Ministry of Infrastructure (MIT). The 15 year duration of the MoU guarantees quality assurance of implemented works over extended periods of time, during which technical issues may emerge and therefore additional costs incurred. The MoU does not prevent Italy and FAO to conclude (overlapping) funding agreements to progressively finance the implementation of the afore-mentioned Masterplan, nor impacts on the work plan of the MIT which is presently consolidating the stone facades of the headquarters buildings.
 
The first contribution for the implementation of EUR 2 Million involves 4 projects as follows:
 
1.	Increase safety of the Plenary Room by restoring the artistic plaster ceiling titled ?Universo? by Mirko Basaldella. Cost estimate: EUR 660 000. Timing estimate: completion in 24 months from the approval by the Italian Authorities.
2.	Consolidation of the wall, surface conservation and clearing of the entire area. Cost estimate: EUR 410 000. Timing estimate: completion in 24 months from the approval by the Italian Authorities.
3.	Structural assessment study of the buildings (A and B) buildings. Cost estimate: EUR 200 000. Timing estimate: completion within 24 months.
4.	Replacement of curt</narrative>
  </description>
